construction of bridges and tunnels crossing the boundary between the United States and Canada. when similar materials are admitted free under similar circumstances into the United States, under regulations prescribed by the Minister;
464. Steel dies, of a class or kind not made in Canada, valued at not less tham one thousand dollars each, for use exclusively in stamping metal sheets or metal plates; Provided that such dies shall be exported from Canada under Customs supervision within three months from the date of import entry;
476. Surgical and dental instruments of any material; surgical needles; X-ray apparatus; surgical operating tables for use in hospitals; microscopes valued at not less than $50 each by retail; and complete parts of all the foregoing;
